# World Bank Indicators API (v2) - canonical calls
# Format: VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP Client (### separates requests).
# Public API: no auth, no key. Never add credentials.
# Grouped by area doc (see README.md). Every request notes what it demonstrates and, where one exists,
# the fixture under samples/ that holds its byte-for-byte response (captured 2026-10-14 UTC).
# Be polite: run requests one at a time; cold cache misses can take 10-40 s.

@base = https://api.worldbank.org/v2
@countries = BRA;CAN;DEU;GBR;IND;JPN;MEX;USA;ZAF
@indicators = SP.POP.TOTL;NY.GDP.MKTP.CD;NY.GDP.PCAP.CD;SP.DYN.LE00.IN
@years = 2018:2024

# ====================================================================================================
# 0. THE PIPELINE RUN - exact calls, in order (README "The pipeline call plan")
# ====================================================================================================

### R0 - Release watermark: WDI lastupdated (assert it equals every observation envelope's lastupdated)
# Envelope page/pages/per_page/total are all STRINGS here. Fixture: samples/metadata/source_2_wdi.json
GET {{base}}/source/2?format=json

### R1 - Income-level reference list (7 rows: HIC INX LIC LMC LMY MIC UMC; LMY/MIC are composites)
# All-string envelope. Fixture: samples/countries/incomeLevel.json
GET {{base}}/incomeLevel?format=json

### R2 - Country dimension for the 9 economies + pre-flight of configured codes
# Current income level / region / lending type; per_page echoed as a STRING; expect exactly 9 rows.
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_9_selected.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}?format=json&per_page=50

### R3 - Indicator metadata: Population, total (assert 1 row and source.id == "2"; unit is "")
# Fixture: samples/metadata/indicator_sp_pop_totl.json
GET {{base}}/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json

### R4 - Indicator metadata: GDP (current US$)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/indicator_ny_gdp_mktp_cd.json
GET {{base}}/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD?format=json

### R5 - Indicator metadata: GDP per capita (current US$)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/indicator_ny_gdp_pcap_cd.json
GET {{base}}/indicator/NY.GDP.PCAP.CD?format=json

### R6 - Indicator metadata: Life expectancy at birth, total (years)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/indicator_sp_dyn_le00_in.json
GET {{base}}/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?format=json

### R7 - Metadata API: Series (unit, aggregation, licence) + Country (IncomeGroup) + Country-Series notes in one call
# Returns a JSON OBJECT, total = 300 metatype entries. NEVER send per_page (it splits variables across pages).
# Fixture: samples/metadata/country_series_metadata_9_countries_4_indicators.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/country/{{countries}}/series/{{indicators}}/metadata?format=json

### R8 - Observations: SP.POP.TOTL, 9 countries x 2018-2024 -> 1 page, 63 rows (all int tokens)
# Fixture (golden): samples/observations/SP.POP.TOTL__9_countries__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### R9 - Observations: NY.GDP.MKTP.CD -> 63 rows; USA values are int tokens, others floats (land as DOUBLE)
# Fixture (golden): samples/observations/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD__9_countries__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### R10 - Observations: NY.GDP.PCAP.CD -> 63 rows (decimal:1)
# Fixture (golden): samples/observations/NY.GDP.PCAP.CD__9_countries__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/NY.GDP.PCAP.CD?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### R11 - Observations: SP.DYN.LE00.IN -> 63 rows (decimal:0 although values have up to 13 decimals)
# Fixture (golden): samples/observations/SP.DYN.LE00.IN__9_countries__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### R1b (optional) - Region labels: 44 rows, different record shape (id/code/iso2code/name)
# Fixture: samples/countries/region.json
GET {{base}}/region?format=json&per_page=100

### R1c (optional) - Lending-type labels: 4 rows
# Fixture: samples/countries/lendingType.json
GET {{base}}/lendingType?format=json

### R12 (optional benchmark) - WB income-group aggregates as "countries": 28 rows, countryiso3code "" (map via XD/XT/XN/XM)
# Uses CURRENT membership for every year. Fixture: samples/countries/income_aggregates_SP.POP.TOTL.json
GET {{base}}/country/HIC;UMC;LMC;LIC/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=100

### R13 (optional benchmark) - income-group aggregates, GDP (aggregation: gap-filled total). Cold miss took 45.2 s.
# Fixture: samples/countries/income_aggregates_NY.GDP.MKTP.CD.json
GET {{base}}/country/HIC;UMC;LMC;LIC/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=100

### R14 (optional benchmark) - income-group aggregates, GDP per capita (aggregation: weighted average)
# Fixture: samples/countries/income_aggregates_NY.GDP.PCAP.CD.json
GET {{base}}/country/HIC;UMC;LMC;LIC/indicator/NY.GDP.PCAP.CD?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=100

### R15 (optional benchmark) - income-group aggregates, life expectancy (aggregation: weighted average)
# Fixture: samples/countries/income_aggregates_SP.DYN.LE00.IN.json
GET {{base}}/country/HIC;UMC;LMC;LIC/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=100

# ====================================================================================================
# 1. COUNTRIES, REGIONS, INCOME LEVELS (01_countries_and_classifications.md)
# ====================================================================================================

### 1.1 Single country by ISO3
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_single_BRA.json
GET {{base}}/country/BRA?format=json

### 1.2 Single country by lower-case ISO2 - byte-identical to 1.1 (codes are case-insensitive)
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_single_br_iso2_lower.json
GET {{base}}/country/br?format=json

### 1.3 Mixed ISO2/ISO3, mixed case, shuffled order - returned sorted by id (BRA, DEU, USA, ZAF)
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_mixed_iso2_iso3_reordered.json
GET {{base}}/country/zaf;US;de;BRA?format=json

### 1.4 date= is IGNORED on /country (byte-identical to 1.1): no historical income classification exists here
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_BRA_with_date_param.json
GET {{base}}/country/BRA?format=json&date=2018

### 1.5 Aggregates through /country: region.id "NA", lendingType.id "", lat/long ""
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_aggregates_WLD_HIC_EUU.json
GET {{base}}/country/WLD;HIC;EUU?format=json

### 1.6 Full country list, page 1 of 3 at per_page=100 (296 rows = 217 economies + 79 aggregates)
# Fixtures: samples/countries/country_all_per_page_100_page{1,2,3}.json
GET {{base}}/country?format=json&per_page=100&page=1

### 1.7 Full country list, last page (96 rows)
GET {{base}}/country?format=json&per_page=100&page=3

### 1.8 Current members of an income level (HIC: 86 economies in the API vs 87 on the WB page)
# Fixture: samples/countries/incomeLevel_HIC_country.json
GET {{base}}/incomeLevel/HIC/country?format=json&per_page=100

### 1.9 Same via query argument - byte-identical to 1.8
GET {{base}}/country?incomeLevel=HIC&format=json&per_page=100

### 1.10 Single income level
# Fixture: samples/countries/incomeLevel_UMC_single.json
GET {{base}}/incomeLevel/UMC?format=json

### 1.11 Single region - note the trailing space in "Latin America & Caribbean "
# Fixture: samples/countries/region_LCN_single.json
GET {{base}}/region/LCN?format=json

### 1.12 GOTCHA: lending-type member filter returns every economy TWICE (total 134, 67 unique ids)
# Fixture: samples/countries/lendingType_IBD_country_duplicates.json
GET {{base}}/lendingType/IBD/country?format=json&per_page=200

### 1.13 DO NOT USE: language prefix translates names AND capitalCity (ZAF "Ciudad del Cabo")
# Fixture: samples/countries/country_9_selected_es.json (holds 3 countries despite its name)
GET {{base}}/es/country/BRA;DEU;ZAF?format=json

### 1.14 WDI country metadata: IncomeGroup with no year dimension (top-level JSON OBJECT)
# Fixture: samples/countries/sources2_country_BRA_metadata.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/country/BRA/metadata?format=json

### 1.15 Join keys: observation country.id is ISO2 ("BR"), countryiso3code is ISO3 ("BRA")
# Fixture: samples/countries/indicator_BRA_join_key_demo.json
GET {{base}}/country/BRA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2024

### 1.16 Evidence that WB aggregates use CURRENT membership (sum of current LIC/LMC/UMC members == aggregate, 2018)
# Fixture: samples/countries/indicator_all_SP.POP.TOTL_2018_membership_check.json (53 KB)
GET {{base}}/country/all/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2018&per_page=400

# ====================================================================================================
# 2. INDICATOR OBSERVATIONS (02_indicator_observations.md)
# ====================================================================================================

### 2.1 Baseline: 1 country x 1 indicator, 7 rows (date is a quoted string, value a number)
# Fixture: samples/observations/single_country_single_indicator__USA__SP.POP.TOTL__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/USA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=50

### 2.2 Multi-indicator (needs source=2): 252 rows == union of R8-R11, but meta.sourceid is null. Not recommended.
# Fixture: samples/observations/multi_indicator__4_indicators__9_countries__2018_2024__source2.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/{{indicators}}?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### 2.3 Multi-indicator WITHOUT source -> HTTP 200 + error 120
# Fixture: samples/observations/error__multi_indicator_without_source__http200_error_120.json
GET {{base}}/country/ZAF;USA;MEX;JPN;IND;GBR;DEU;CAN;BRA/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN;NY.GDP.PCAP.CD;NY.GDP.MKTP.CD;SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### 2.4 Ordering: reversed country list still comes back BRA..ZAF (sorted by ISO3, then date desc)
# Fixture: samples/observations/ordering__countries_reversed__SP.POP.TOTL__2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/ZAF;USA;MEX;JPN;IND;GBR;DEU;CAN;BRA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2024&per_page=1000

### 2.5 Sort key is ISO3, not ISO2: AUT;AUS returns AUS first
# Fixture: samples/observations/verify__sort_key_is_iso3__SP.POP.TOTL__AUT_AUS__2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/AUT;AUS/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2024

### 2.6 Lower-case ISO2 + lower-case indicator accepted; canonical ids echoed back
# Fixture: samples/observations/codes__iso2_lowercase__sp.pop.totl__2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/br;ca;de;gb;in;jp;mx;us;za/indicator/sp.pop.totl?format=json&date=2024&per_page=1000

### 2.7 MISSING DATA: 2025 rows come back with value:null (reported_null); 2026 rows are ABSENT (not_returned)
# Fixture: samples/observations/date_range_beyond_latest__SP.DYN.LE00.IN__9_countries__2023_2026.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?format=json&date=2023:2026&per_page=1000

### 2.8 MISSING DATA in the recommended call shape (single indicator, source=2)
# Fixture: samples/observations/verify__null_rows_single_indicator_source2__SP.DYN.LE00.IN__BRA_USA__2024_2026.json
GET {{base}}/country/BRA;USA/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?source=2&format=json&date=2024:2026&per_page=1000

### 2.9 MISSING DATA (out-of-scope sparse series): Gini, 25 of 63 in-range cells are null rows
# Fixture: samples/observations/missing_data_example__SI.POV.GINI__9_countries__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SI.POV.GINI?format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### 2.10 Years just past scope: 2025 published for POP/GDP/PCAP, null for LE; 2026 absent; null rows carry "scale":""
# Fixture: samples/observations/out_of_scope_years__4_indicators__9_countries__2025_2026__source2.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/{{indicators}}?source=2&format=json&date=2025:2026&per_page=1000

### 2.11 Reversed date range is normalised (same rows as 2018:2024)
# Fixture: samples/observations/date_range_reversed__USA__SP.POP.TOTL__2024_2018.json
GET {{base}}/country/USA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2024:2018

### 2.12 source=2 on a single-indicator call: byte-identical to the call without it (source is a no-op here)
# Fixture: samples/observations/single_indicator_with_source2__NY.GDP.MKTP.CD__9_countries_reversed__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/ZAF;USA;MEX;JPN;IND;GBR;DEU;CAN;BRA/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD?source=2&format=json&date={{years}}&per_page=1000

### 2.13 DO NOT USE: mrv overrides date (returns 2025, outside 2018:2024)
# Fixture: samples/observations/verify__mrv_overrides_date__SP.POP.TOTL__GBR_IND__date_2018_2024_mrv_2.json
GET {{base}}/country/GBR;IND/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&mrv=2

### 2.14 DO NOT USE: mrnev hides gaps; sourceid null and rows have no "unit" key
# Fixture: samples/observations/verify__mrnev_2_rows_have_no_unit_key__SP.DYN.LE00.IN__CAN_DEU.json
GET {{base}}/country/CAN;DEU/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?format=json&mrnev=2

### 2.15 DO NOT USE: gapfill fabricates 2025 values (copies 2024) with obs_status ""
# Fixture: samples/observations/verify__gapfill_fabricates_2025__SP.DYN.LE00.IN__IND_ZAF.json
GET {{base}}/country/IND;ZAF/indicator/SP.DYN.LE00.IN?format=json&mrv=2&gapfill=Y

### 2.16 DO NOT USE: scale=y is lossy (USA GDP 2024 -> value 29, scale "trillions")
# Fixture: samples/observations/optional_param__scale_y__USA__NY.GDP.MKTP.CD__2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/USA/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.CD?format=json&date=2024&scale=y

### 2.17 footnote=y adds a "footnote" key to every row ("" for USA population)
# Fixture: samples/observations/optional_param__footnote_y__USA__SP.POP.TOTL__2018_2024.json
GET {{base}}/country/USA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&footnote=y

### 2.18 Non-empty obs_status exists in other sources ("F" = forecast, source 27) - never seen in scope
# Fixture: samples/observations/obs_status_example__CHN__NYGDPMKTPKDZ__mrv3.json
GET {{base}}/country/CHN/indicator/NYGDPMKTPKDZ?format=json&mrv=3

### 2.19 Default format is XML when format= is omitted
# Fixture: samples/observations/format_default_xml__USA__SP.POP.TOTL__2024.xml
GET {{base}}/country/USA/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?date=2024

# ====================================================================================================
# 3. INDICATOR & SOURCE METADATA, FRESHNESS (03_indicator_and_source_metadata.md)
# ====================================================================================================

### 3.1 Semicolon list on /indicator is NOT supported: HTTP 200, total 0, [] (assert 1 row per code)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/indicator_multi_semicolon_returns_empty.json
GET {{base}}/indicator/{{indicators}}?format=json

### 3.2 Metadata API, series only (4 series, 60 metatype entries; per_page "5000" default)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/series_metadata_4_indicators.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/series/{{indicators}}/metadata?format=json

### 3.3 GOTCHA: per_page IS honoured by the Metadata API and splits a variable across pages
# Fixtures: samples/metadata/series_metadata_4_indicators_per_page_10_page_{1,2}.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/series/{{indicators}}/metadata?format=json&per_page=10

### 3.4 Metadata API IncomeGroup only (current classification, no year)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/country_incomegroup_metatype_9_countries.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/country/{{countries}}/metatypes/incomegroup/metadata?format=json

### 3.5 Footnote metadata (undocumented path) - DEU population "Break in series." 2022/2023
# Fixture: samples/metadata/footnote_metadata_deu_sp_pop_totl_2022_2023.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/footnote/DEU~SP.POP.TOTL~YR2022;DEU~SP.POP.TOTL~YR2023/metadata?format=json

### 3.6 Footnote metadata, no footnote -> HTTP 200 text/xml error id 160 even with format=json
# Fixture: samples/metadata/footnote_metadata_usa_sp_pop_totl_2020_not_found.xml
GET {{base}}/sources/2/footnote/USA~SP.POP.TOTL~YR2020/metadata?format=json

### 3.7 Invalid series on the Metadata API -> HTTP 200 text/xml error id 160
# Fixture: samples/metadata/series_metadata_invalid_code_xml_error.xml
GET {{base}}/sources/2/series/NOT.A.CODE/metadata?format=json

### 3.8 Observations with footnote=y: DEU 2022/2023 "Break in series."
# Fixture: samples/metadata/data_sp_pop_totl_9_countries_2018_2024_footnote_y.json
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&footnote=y&per_page=100

### 3.9 Docs vs live: footnote=n does NOT remove footnotes (served from cache, plain application/json)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/data_sp_pop_totl_deu_2022_2023_footnote_n.json
GET {{base}}/country/DEU/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date=2022:2023&footnote=n

### 3.10 Conditional request: If-Modified-Since -> 304 from Cloudflare (cache state, NOT a data-change signal)
# Headers: samples/metadata/headers_conditional_if_modified_since_data_304.txt
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&footnote=y&per_page=100
If-Modified-Since: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:12:36 GMT

### 3.11 No ETag support: If-None-Match: * -> 200 with full body
# Headers: samples/metadata/headers_conditional_if_none_match_star_200.txt
GET {{base}}/country/{{countries}}/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json&date={{years}}&footnote=y&per_page=100
If-None-Match: *

### 3.12 Sources list (71 sources; all-string envelope)
# Fixture: samples/metadata/sources_list_per_page_100.json
GET {{base}}/sources?format=json&per_page=100

### 3.13 Source 2 concepts (Country, Series, Time) - JSON OBJECT envelope, per_page a number
# Fixture: samples/metadata/source_2_concepts.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/concepts?format=json

### 3.14 Advanced Data API (BETA) - also carries lastupdated
# Fixture: samples/metadata/advanced_data_deu_sp_pop_totl_2023.json
GET {{base}}/sources/2/country/DEU/series/SP.POP.TOTL/time/yr2023/data?format=json

### 3.15 Unversioned (v1-style) path -> 301 to /v2 with a text body (docs say "Resource not found")
# Fixture: samples/metadata/unversioned_path_redirect_301.txt
# @no-redirect
GET https://api.worldbank.org/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL?format=json

### 3.16 Successor platform Data360 (different host and schema; OBS_VALUE is a string) - comparison only
# Fixture: samples/metadata/data360_wdi_sp_pop_totl_deu_top10.json
GET https://data360api.worldbank.org/data360/data?DATABASE_ID=WB_WDI&INDICATOR=WB_WDI_SP_POP_TOTL&REF_AREA=DEU&top=10

